{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% from "hero.njk" import hero %}
{% from "section.njk" import section %}
{% from "section-header.njk" import sectionHeader %}
{% from "section-body.njk" import sectionBody %}
{% from "section-visual.njk" import sectionVisual %}
{% from "two-block-header.njk" import twoBlockHeader %}
{% from "gallery-navigation.njk" import galleryNavigation %}
{% from "scene-gallery.njk" import sceneGallery %}

{% block body %}
<main>
  {# 1. Hero #}
  {{ hero(
    "../../assets/illustrations/bill-pay/hero/bill-pay-hero-illustration.png",
    "Lorem ipsum is a dummy placeholder text <br /><br />It lets people view page layouts and fonts without getting ",
    "When simplicity is not the right design strategy",
    "Lorem ipsum is a dummy placeholder text used in design and publishing. It lets people view page layouts and fonts without being distracted by real words."
  ) }}

  {# 2. Section header with subheading, no visual #}
  {% call section() %}
  {{ sectionHeader("Money on the move", "Business background") }}
  {{ sectionBody([
    "For decades, QuickBooks has been the accounting tool for a large share of American small businesses. Invoices, bills, reconciliation, the ledger - numbers lived in QuickBooks, yet, for just as long, the actual money movement happened elsewhere. When it came down to payments, users would open their bank portals, write checks, or rely on whatever third-party workarounds they could grab.",
    "This led to a fragmented experience, as QuickBooks forced its customers to manually record the payment outcome, resulting in sync latency and data mismatches. For an accounting platform, it’s a huge deal, as this was exactly what it was supposed to prevent.",
    "QuickBooks started closing that gap by integrating payment capabilities natively into the platform. First, it was invoices (AR); then came the bill payments capability (AP), with a mission to capture the entire bill lifecycle within a single, seamless workflow."
  ]) }}
  {% endcall %}

  {# 3. Gallery section #}
  {% call section("section--grey-light") %}
  {{ sectionHeader("Click, Click, Done", "Exiting Experience") }}
  {# Gallery intro paragraph moved to statBlock above #}
  {% call sectionVisual(true) %}
  <div class="gallery">
    <iframe class="gallery__visual" id="gallery-visual" title="Walkthrough step"></iframe>
    {{ galleryNavigation("gallery") }}
  </div>
  {% endcall %}
  {{ sectionBody([
    "Bill Pay V1 was designed to meet the needs of QuickBooks's core audience, small business owners, handling their own books, and processing up to 30 bills a month.",
    "The overhead of moving money was wrapped inside a friendly, linear wizard with clean UI and low cognitive load. Paying a bill to a vendor was easy like ordering pizza. It was also totally unprepared for its next growth opportunity, already hiding inside the ecosystem."
  ]) }}
  {% endcall %}

  {# 4. Tipping Point — one section, two visual blocks (white then green).
     White block: real bill-pay-stat image + its intro copy, appended via
     firstExtra right after the existing body paragraph.
     Green block: real team-members image, unchanged. #}
  {% set statBlock %}
  {{ sectionBody([
    "A year after V1's launch, money was moving comfortably on rails, the product was buzzing and gaining traction with small businesses, when, one day, product analysts walked into the room, and pointed to a single statistic that changed the conversation.",
    "It was a classic 80/20 rule in its most painful version. A tiny group of customers, representing less than a quarter of the platform base, was sitting on more than 90% of the total potential payment volume. The potential was obvious, so was the problem, as these weren't the customers Bill Pay had been built for."
  ]) }}
  <div class="section-image-group">
    <img class="section-image-group__image" src="../../assets/illustrations/bill-pay/bill-pay-stat.png" alt="" />
  </div>
  {% endset %}
  {% call twoBlockHeader(
    "Tipping Point",
    "Mission & Scope",
    [],
    [],
    "section--green-light",
    "",
    statBlock
  ) %}
  {{ sectionBody([
    "High-Value Billers were Mid-Market companies processing hundreds, even thousands, of bills monthly. They used QuickBooks for accounting, and were recording their bills on the platform, but still were leaking out to execute payments, as the product could not support their scale.",
    "The team went on an early discovery, trying to map out the gaps. They met with AP teams who walked them through their bill-payment workflows, and reviewed the current solution. The interviewees looked at that beautiful, sequential, multi-step wizard and said, \"Guys, we love you, but we're not going to use your payment product.\""
  ]) }}
  <div class="section-image-group">
    <img class="section-image-group__image" src="../../assets/illustrations/bill-pay/team-members.png" alt="" />
  </div>
  {{ sectionBody([
    "Two things became clear. First, a linear flow was like asking them to fill an Olympic pool with a spoon. Second, and most importantly, payment execution at scale meant a multi-seat operation and segregation of duty. So what would it take to scale this lightweight payment feature into a Mid-Market AP machine?",
    "The required capabilities were scattered across legacy domains, none of them were built to work together the way this workflow demanded, and they were guarded by different teams and organizations across QuickBooks. Building all these capabilities went far beyond Bill Pay.",
    "Now, the team also had to drive this alignment puzzle, where multiple teams, each with their own metrics and roadmaps, needs to move in the same direction at the same time.",
    "Leadership said go, and I was brought in as Principal Designer. My mission was to partner with design and cross-functional leads across QuickBooks, to rethink our core capabilities, while building a new Bill Pay experience that serves payment execution at scale."
  ]) }}
  {{ sectionBody(["role:", "role:", "role:", "role:"]) }}
  {% endcall %}

  {# 5. Cockpit Widget section — header, body, widget, then a second trailing body #}
  {% call section() %}
  {{ sectionHeader("Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet", "Lorem ipsum elephant") }}
  {{ sectionBody(["Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua."]) }}
  {% call sectionVisual(true) %}
  <div class="cockpit-widget">
    <div class="cockpit-left-nav">
      <div class="cockpit-nav-panel">
        <div class="cockpit-headline-row">
          <h2 class="cockpit-headline">AP workflow, Journey & Empathy Mapping</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="cockpit-content-row">
          <div class="cockpit-steps-column-wrapper">
            <div class="cockpit-selected-bg" id="cockpit-selected-bg"></div>
            <div class="cockpit-connector-line"></div>
            <ol class="cockpit-steps-column" id="cockpit-steps-column"></ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cockpit-toggle-slot">
        <div class="cockpit-toggle" id="cockpit-toggle">
          <div class="cockpit-toggle__track journey" id="cockpit-toggle-track">
            <div class="cockpit-toggle__pill"></div>
            <p class="cockpit-toggle__label" id="cockpit-toggle-label-journey">Journey</p>
            <p class="cockpit-toggle__label" id="cockpit-toggle-label-empathy">Empathy</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cockpit-right" id="cockpit-right">
      <div class="cockpit-members-rail" id="cockpit-members-rail">
        <div class="cockpit-member-row" id="cockpit-member-row"></div>
        <div class="cockpit-highlight-track">
          <div class="cockpit-highlight-track__fill" id="cockpit-highlight-fill"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endcall %}
  {{ sectionBody(["Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident."]) }}
  {% endcall %}

  {# 6. The AP manager #}
  {% call section("section--grey-light") %}
  {{ sectionHeader("The AP manager") }}
  {{ sectionVisual() }}
  {{ sectionBody(["Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit."]) }}
  {% endcall %}

  {# 7. Designing a cockpit — header block (white) + continuation (green, scene gallery) #}
  {% call twoBlockHeader(
    "Designing a cockpit",
    "",
    ["Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit."]
  ) %}
  {{ sceneGallery() }}
  {% endcall %}
</main>
{% endblock %}
